at all costs.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.634
It's time
for the latest installment of my

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.133
Do Not Read list.
Here we go.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:12.501
♪ Do not read, do not read ♪

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.868
♪ Do not read these books,
these books ♪

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.200
-Now, before we start,
I just want you to know

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.801
that every book that I'm about
to show you is 100% real.

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.734
These are actual books that
you can find them on Amazon

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.734
or check them out
at your local library.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.033
They are real.

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.200
All right, let's see what's on
my Do Not Read list.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.934
This first one is a joke book.
-Oh, great.

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.634
Love jokes.
-Yeah, that's right up my alley.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:33.567
This one's called
"The Humour of Germany."

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:38.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.501
Well, it's a hilarious cover.
Already, the cover's funny.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:42.067
-Yeah.
What year was --

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.100
I just want to know
what year that's from.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.567
-They have some classics
in here.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:46.901
-Oh, okay.
-Yeah, here.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.334
How about this classic
right here?

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.234
A chapter -- "The Incarceration
of Herr Professor."

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.467
Sounds hilarious.
I'll give it a read.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.634
-[ German accent ] It's funny!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:57.801
-Next up is a cookbook.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:58.934
-[ Normal voice ]
Oh, I love cookbooks.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:00:59.934
-I have a great collection
of cookbooks.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:01.167
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.200
This one is
"500 Tasty Sandwich Recipes."

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.234
-Mmm.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.601
-Look at how tasty
that one looks.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.133
[ Laughter and groans ]

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.267
-Oh!

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:12.267
Wow!
What?

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.100
That's a sandwich?
-A good asparagus sandwich.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.734
-Mmm!
-Open face.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.968
-Oh, put it in the toaster oven.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.534
-Name what sandwich that is.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:23.300
[ Laughter ]
-Oh. The pimento loaf --

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.434
-There's a surprise at the end.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.067
What do they have in here?
-It's called da laundry lint.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.234
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.834
Oh, my goodness.
Look at this.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.367
They have
ham and peanut butter sandwich.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.934
-Oh.
-Ham and raisin.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.701
Pot--
Potted meat.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:38.734
-Ugh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.667
Mmm, tasty!
-That's pretty good.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.400
Potted meat, yeah.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.434
Next up is an activity book
for kids.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:45.467
-Oh, great.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.067
-It's called "101 Things
for Girls To Do."

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.667
-Mm-hmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:52.534
-I have girls.
This might be great for them.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:57.033
-What can they do?
-Let's see what they can do.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.300
How to sharpen scissors.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.534
-What?

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.834
And then run with them.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:07.934
There's other things to do.
There's other things to do.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.968
Next up is a travel book.
-Oh, I love travel.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.334
-A lot of people are looking
forward to just

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.234
getting out there traveling,
people who are looking

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.234
to take the family road trip.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.000
Check this out here.
This is called

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.501
"Nuclear Heartland:
A guide to the 1,000

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:21.834
Missile Silos
of the United States."

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.100
-Mm.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.067
I can't wait.
-Let's take a look inside here.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:27.567
This one says,
"A Family Outing," here.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.968
It says, "A Family Outing."

00:02:29.968 --> 00:02:33.234
"We sat, my wife, our three
children, myself, and our dog.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.601
A few hundred feet away
was a Minuteman missile

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.167
tipped with a warhead
containing an explosive force

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.334
of 1.2 million tons of TNT.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:42.901
It hummed during the night."

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.000
Sounds like a dream family vac--

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.701
You won't forget
that vacation too soon.

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.968
-No, it'll be -- every time
the child closes his eyes,

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.801
he'll remember that vacation.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.400
"Why am I radioactive?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.467
-All right.
Next is a cookbook called

00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:00.234
"Cooking with Coke."
-Oh, is it by Don Jr.?

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:01.934
[ Laughter ]
-No, it's --

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:10.434
♪♪

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.801
-Coca-Cola.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:13.868
No, the soft --

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.100
"Cooking with --"
"Cooking with Coke."

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.601
Yeah, here we go.
"Cooking with Coca-Cola."

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.000
-Coca-Cola, okay.
-"Cooking with Coke."

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.801
-My mistake.
-"Cooking with Coke."

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.300
-I feel like
a real Peter Douchey.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.767
-Here's a, uh --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.868
-Doocy.
-Doocy, sorry.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.767
Here's a recipe.
Here's sweet and spicy

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.667
shrimp tacos with mango salsa.
-Mmm.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.634
-Uh, I don't know about
the mango salsa.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:37.267
I don't want
the mango overpowering

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:41.734
the shrimp and Coke.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.534
'Cause that's just a combo.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:44.934
-That's up there with, like,
ham and raisins.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:47.801
-Yeah, I love ham, raisins,
and Coke.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.100
-We're down to our last book.
It's a self-help book.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.801
-Oh, I love self-help.
-Yeah.

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:55.501
This is called "A Guided
Meditation for Beginners."

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.734
-Oh, that's great.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:57.834
-We could all use this
right now.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:58.968
-Yeah.
-Let's see what tips

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:01.200
they have for us here.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.767
-Okay. What's page one?
-Here we go.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.834
This first page says, "Inhale."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:10.000
-Okay.
-Next one says, "Exhale."

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.434
